     'I hope you and uncle are doing well. We have just returned from a wonderful trip to Coorg (Kodagu) during the Sankranti holidays. I want to share my experience with you.\n'
     'Coorg lies midway between Mysuru and Mangaluru. It is the smallest district of Karnataka, full of evergreen rainforests, coffee estates and spice plantations. '
     'The weather was cool and pleasant, and the air was filled with the smell of coffee.\n'
     'We stayed in a homestay. The Kodavu people were very hospitable and told us stories of their valour. We learnt that Coorg gave India its first Commander-in-Chief, General K.M. Cariappa, and that the Coorg Regiment is one of the most decorated in the army.\n'
